{
  "description": "Five copies of the Damaged Helmet, from one import and one copy of its 3.7 MB of geometry and textures. The helmet is imported, never restated: each plinth names it with a core::child reference, and composing writes a glTF node per relation, so the helmet is written once per placement while its mesh, images and buffer stay single. Two plinths make a pair, two rows each hold that pair -- so the pair, both plinths and the helmet beneath them are written once per row -- and a fifth placement stands on its own, turned a quarter turn. Regenerate the import it needs with:  mosaic gltf-pack gltf/DamagedHelmet.glb helmet.tsr --stable-ids  -- the stable ids are what let this file name a node inside it.",
